{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "action": "answer",
  "response": null,
  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "c1",
      "text": "The monitoring stack includes Grafana for watching deployments and operational metrics.",
      "citation_ids": ["S1"]
    },
    {
      "id": "c2",
      "text": "Argo CD (core/headless install) was used to provision the cluster state as code, keeping it identical to git with automated sync, selfHeal, and prune capabilities.",
      "citation_ids": ["S2"]
    },
    {
      "id": "c3",
      "text": "A dedicated read-only deploy key is used for repo access in Argo CD, adhering to least privilege principles without using account credentials.",
      "citation_ids": ["S2"]
    },
    {
      "id": "c4",
      "text": "Live behavior verified includes manual cluster sabotage (Grafana scaled to 0) being reverted by Argo CD selfHeal in 10 seconds.",
      "citation_ids": ["S2"]
    },
    {
      "id": "c5",
      "text": "A git-only label change was verified to arrive on-cluster within one poll cycle (197s) with no human action required.",
      "citation_ids": ["S2"]
    },
    {
      "id": "c6",
      "text": "Operational consequence of the setup is that ad-hoc kubectl edits are reverted by Argo CD, ensuring only git changes persist.",
      "citation_ids": ["S2"]
    }
  ]
}

